  <h2>1. Executive Summary</h2>
  <p>Modern Enterprise Resource Planning (ERP) environments process vast volumes of sensitive financial, procurement, and human resource transactions. Traditional rule-based ERP security models suffer from two critical vulnerabilities:</p>
  <ul>
    <li><strong>Alert Fatigue &amp; Overflagging:</strong> Up to 85% of standard rule-based alerts represent benign operational spikes (e.g., month-end financial closing).</li>
    <li><strong>Multi-Turn Conversational Exfiltration:</strong> Adversaries use multi-step natural language interfaces to extract sensitive PII and financial records piecemeal without triggering single-request rule thresholds.</li>
  </ul>
  <p>This document details an <strong>AI-Powered ERP Threat Defense Framework</strong> combining 9-tier anomaly detection, dynamic context enrichment, stateful session monitoring, and FinOps cloud cost correlation.</p>

