  <h2>4. Core Mathematical Formulations</h2>
  <h3>Statistical Anomaly (Z-Score)</h3>
  <p>Measures parametric deviation from a rolling historical baseline profile:</p>
  <pre>Z = (x - μ) / σ</pre>

  <h3>Context-Adjusted Thresholds</h3>
  <p>Prevents alert floods during known business events by dynamically scaling limits:</p>
  <pre>T_Adjusted = T_Base * (1 + δ_Calendar) * (1 + δ_Role)</pre>

  <h3>Cross-Domain Unified Risk Aggregation</h3>
  <p>Integrates security telemetry, application logs, cloud compute loads, and billing metrics:</p>
  <pre>R_Unified = (w1 * R_Security) + (w2 * R_ERP) + (w3 * R_Cloud) + (w4 * R_FinOps)</pre>

  <h2>5. SOC Automation Playbook Rules</h2>
  <ul>
    <li><strong>Low Risk (&lt; 40):</strong> Allow transaction execution, write record to immutable audit storage, update baseline metrics.</li>
    <li><strong>Medium Risk (40 - 74):</strong> Pause thread, issue FIDO2/TOTP step-up MFA challenge to user device. On verification, resume; on failure, escalate to 85.</li>
    <li><strong>High Risk (&ge; 75):</strong> Terminate OAuth2 session, revoke active bearer tokens, freeze database transaction execution, write high-priority incident payload to SIEM/SOAR platform.</li>
  </ul>

